The attached image, Figure 10, illustrates the local inflammatory response and uptake of Nano-11 by immune cells 24 hours after intramuscular injection in mouse skeletal muscle. The top row, showing Nano-11 with OVA, reveals significant infiltration of Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages and MHCII+ cells, which actively phagocytized the red-labeled Nano-11 (indicated by arrows and colocalization). In contrast, the bottom row, representing soluble OVA alone, shows minimal inflammatory cell recruitment and no Nano-11. This demonstrates Nano-11's ability to induce a localized inflammatory response, recruit antigen-presenting cells, and facilitate antigen uptake, key mechanisms for its adjuvant effect as described in the PDF.